From 05734dbe9a80fb87d16b6e7035e30a5de1544c0b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yaron Shahrabani <EMAIL>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 08:30:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] media: venus: helpers: report the full frame size for
 encoder input

Clients such as GStreamer set bytesused of a raw NV12 input frame to
the visible image size (460800 bytes for 640x480), while the HFI 1.x
firmware (MSM8916, VIDEO.VE.1.8) expects at least its own frame size
including the stride and scanline padding (460928 bytes) and aborts the
session ("Err_Fatal - venus/utils/src/vbuffer.c:1322") when the filled
length is shorter. v4l2-ctl, which fills the whole buffer, is not
affected.

For encoder input buffers, pass the firmware frame size as the filled
length when the payload is shorter but the buffer is large enough.

Fixes: aaaa93eda64b ("[media] media: venus: venc: add video encoder files")
Assisted-by: claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/helpers.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/helpers.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/helpers.c
index 59eee3d..0649ddb 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/helpers.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/helpers.c
@@ -516,6 +516,18 @@ session_process_buf(struct venus_inst *inst, struct vb2_v4l2_buffer *vbuf)
 		fdata.filled_len = vb2_get_plane_payload(vb, 0);
 		fdata.offset = vb->planes[0].data_offset;
 
+		/*
+		 * Userspace counts only the visible pixels of a raw frame
+		 * (e.g. 460800 bytes for 640x480 NV12), but the HFI 1.x firmware
+		 * checks the filled length against its own frame size including
+		 * the stride/scanline padding (460928 here) and aborts the
+		 * session when it is shorter. Report the full frame.
+		 */
+		if (inst->session_type == VIDC_SESSION_TYPE_ENC &&
+		    fdata.filled_len && fdata.filled_len < inst->input_buf_size &&
+		    inst->input_buf_size <= fdata.alloc_len)
+			fdata.filled_len = inst->input_buf_size;
+
 		if (vbuf->flags & V4L2_BUF_FLAG_LAST || !fdata.filled_len)
 			fdata.flags |= HFI_BUFFERFLAG_EOS;
 
